  <chapter xml:id="chapter_scope">
    <title>Scope</title>
    <para>This document classifies ONVIF device metrics into IANA public OIDs, derived public OIDs, and metrics published under the ONVIF private enterprise number (PEN 66630).</para>
  </chapter>
  <chapter xml:id="chapter_legend">
    <title>Classification Legend</title>
    <itemizedlist>
      <listitem><para><emphasis role="bold">IANA Public OID</emphasis> – the metric maps directly to an object defined in a standard (IANA-registered) MIB. (<xref linkend="chapter_iana"/>, 44 metrics)</para></listitem>
      <listitem><para><emphasis role="bold">Public OID (Derived)</emphasis> – the metric is computed from, or inferred from, one or more standard OIDs. (<xref linkend="chapter_derived"/>, 8 metrics)</para></listitem>
      <listitem><para><emphasis role="bold">Gap – IANA Submission Needed</emphasis> – no standard OID exists. Published under the ONVIF private enterprise OID (PEN 66630). (<xref linkend="chapter_pen"/>, 20 metrics)</para></listitem>
    </itemizedlist>
  </chapter>
